Interviewer #1: Mom
Date: 10/28/2026

Questions & Answers

Q1: Have you experienced any natural disasters before (Tornadoes, Earthquakes, Hurricanes, Floodings, Droughts, etc.)? If so, what was it?

A: Hurricane Sandy and Hurricane Irene

Q2: What situation were you in when that disaster struck?

A: I was visiting my cousin’s house in Upstate New York when Hurricane Irene struck. For Hurricane Sandy, we (me, my son, my husband, my mother, and my husband’s uncle) were all home. We had no power for 4 days.

Q3: How did you find out that the disaster was approaching you? News? App? Didn’t know?

A: From the news.

Q4: When you got hit, did you experience any damage to your property? Or any property damage outside your house?

A: Hurricane Irene damaged a small corner outside of the house, electricity went in and out. For Sandy, we had no power for 4 days, we threw all of our food in the fridge away. My husband’s restaurant in Manhattan had no electricity for two weeks, my brother in New Jersey also had no power for two weeks.

Q5: Did anyone you know also get affected by this disaster? If so, is there anyone else you think I could speak with?

A: My husband’s restaurant and my brother in Jersey, that’s all I know. They had no power for two weeks because of Hurricane Sandy.


Synthesis
One surprising quote: “We had no power for 4 days.”
 
One thing you didn’t expect: The amount of damage Hurricane Sandy caused

What this makes you think about your problem?: Powerful hurricanes like Sandy should be documented before they make landfall so people can get prepared properly.



